Iris Flower Classification Using Machine Learning
1. Project Overview

This project uses Machine Learning to classify Iris flowers into three species: Setosa, Versicolor, and Virginica. The model predicts the flower species based on sepal and petal measurements.

2. Project Objectives
Understand and explore a dataset using Python.
Visualize flower measurements using graphs.
Train a Machine Learning classification model.
Evaluate model performance using accuracy and a confusion matrix.
Predict the species of a new flower.
3. Technologies Used
Python
Pandas
Matplotlib
Scikit-learn
Google Colab
Logistic Regression
4. Dataset Description

The Iris dataset contains 150 flower samples and four input features:

Sepal length (cm)
Sepal width (cm)
Petal length (cm)
Petal width (cm)

The target variable contains three species:

Setosa
Versicolor
Virginica
5. Methodology
Load the Iris dataset.
Explore the data and check for missing values.
Visualize the flower measurements.
Split the data into training and testing sets.
Standardize the features and train a Logistic Regression model.
Evaluate the model using accuracy, a classification report, and a confusion matrix.
Test the model with new flower measurements.
6. Model Evaluation

The model was evaluated using a test dataset containing 20% of the samples.

Accuracy: See the actual accuracy score displayed in the project notebook.

The confusion matrix and classification report are included in the notebook outputs.

